    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d146">

                <pb facs="0190" n="180" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg180"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/2–245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-02T19:00:00+01:00">February 2, 1945—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 2—6:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>173. Comea 170. In accordance with instructions received from the Secretary I
                    have today addressed identic letters to the Soviet and UK representatives on the
                    European Advisory Commission informing them of US approval of the protocol on
                    zones of occupation in Germany, of September 12, 194, modified and completed by
                    the agreement regarding amendments to the above-mentioned protocol, of November
                    14, 194.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
